{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1247602-number-of-successes-on-extended-actions-and-spinning-wheel","id":1247602,"title":"Number of successes on extended actions, and Spinning Wheel","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-18T20:44:31-07:00","id":1247602,"title":"Number of successes on extended actions, and Spinning Wheel","content":"Looking at the description of Spinning Wheel (Royal Crown Contract) brought something to my attention, but I\u2019m not sure the issue is specific to Spinning Wheel. It may relate to all extended actions that count successes. But let\u2019s start with Spinning Wheel as an example.<br /> <br /> Spinning Wheel is invoked as an extended, resisted action, pool of Intelligence + Occult + Wyrd - (target\u2019s) Resolve; 10 minute interval; total target\u2019s Resolve or Wyrd (higher) successes required.<br /> <br /> From the description of success: All rolls leading to this event [chosen by the invoker], made by the target or other characters, gain bonus dice equal to the successes rolled to invoke the Contract, while rolls obstructing the event suffer the same as a penalty, to a maximum of +/\u22125.<br /> <br /> Now, if we just count all successes rolled during the entire series of rolls to invoke Spinning Wheel, that\u2019s always going to be at least equal to the higher of the target\u2019s Resolve and Wyrd. High-Wyrd targets will always hit that +/-5 maximum effect.<br /> <br /> Is that the intent? Because it seems to me that we should be able to have extended actions with relative low success counts.<br /> <br /> (And what happens if we have some other extended action with very high numbers of successes to be accumulated, but want to count successes for variable effect? Do we wind up regularly having to deal with 10 or 20 successes on those?)<br /> <br /> It occurs to me that character counting the successes on only the last roll of an extended action, for the purpose of determining a variable effect, would normalise the final success count to be comparable to that for instant actions. If that\u2019s the intent, though, it does not seem to be explicitly determined by the action rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}